course: dictionary
lesson: 10390
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. You find the right one by reading the words around it, which is its context. «In Atlanta, Malachi's stepbrother Trey is the cool kid, and at school Trey ignores him.» Here Trey is a name. The clues are the capital T, and the words stepbrother, kid and him, which tell you Trey is a person.
explain: Trey can also be a noun for a card, a dice face or a domino with three spots. In card games and dice games, a trey is the number three. If a sentence is about cards, dice or dominoes, check whether it means that three-spot face.
explain: In sports talk in the USA, «hit a trey» means score a three-pointer in basketball: a shot from far away that is worth three points. The clue is the game. If the words are about a court, shooting or scoring, trey means that shot.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a different one. If the sentence is about a person, Trey is a name. If it is about cards, dice or a basketball shot, it is the three.
fact: A trey is a card, dice face or domino with three spots.
fact: In basketball talk in the USA, a trey is a shot scored from far away that is worth three points.
fact: Trey is also a boy's name, often used in the USA.
fact: A capital letter is a clue: Trey with a capital T is a name, as in «at school Trey ignores him».
fact: The words around a word tell you which meaning is right, so always read the whole sentence first.
exercise: In «In Atlanta, Malachi's stepbrother Trey is the cool kid», what is Trey? | A card with three spots | *A boy's name | A shot scored from far away | A dice face with six spots
exercise: In a card game you hold a card with three spots. What is it called? | A boy's name | *A trey | A dice of one | A king
exercise: Friends say «hit a trey» about basketball. What does it mean? | Run very fast to the door | Sit down and rest | Miss the ball completely | *Score a three-pointer
test: In a dice game Sam rolls the face with three spots. What is that face called? | A basketball court | A tray | *A trey | A domino of nine
test: Which sentence uses Trey as a name? | «The trey has three spots.» | *«Trey is my cousin, and he lives next door.» | «Trey hit a trey from the far corner.» | «I rolled a trey on the dice.»
exam: Read «In Atlanta, Malachi's stepbrother Trey is the cool kid.» What clues show that Trey is a name and not a card? | Trey is a card with three spots | Trey is a shot in basketball | *He is a stepbrother and a kid, so Trey is a person | Trey is a dice roll
